   457                          ;; RESTART and GRAB:
   458                          ;;
   459                          ;; GRAB checks that the caller passed enough arguments onto the stack. If not,
   460                          ;; it creates a closure, stores all the available arguments in it, points the
   461                          ;; closure code to the instruction just before GRAB (which is assumed to be a
   462                          ;; RESTART), then returns to the caller, as if executing a RETURN instruction.
   463                          ;; When the new closure is called, RESTART will push the arguments onto the
   464                          ;; stack again and fallthrough GRAB.
